    "guide": {
      "schemaVersion": 1,
      "installation": "```sh\nflavor=night\ncurl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \"${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/alacritty/themes/living-code-$flavor.toml\" \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/living-code-theme/alacritty/main/living-code-$flavor.toml\"\n```\n\nThen import it in `alacritty.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[general]\nimport = [\"~/.config/alacritty/themes/living-code-night.toml\"]\n```\n\nIf you set `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, use that path in the `import` line. On Windows the folder is `%APPDATA%\\alacritty\\themes`.",
      "configuration": "See [Alacritty's documentation](https://alacritty.org) for application settings and reload behavior. The activation instructions above identify each supported flavor; keep your other application configuration.",
      "compatibility": "This port supplies theme files for Alacritty, not the application itself. Install the application separately and follow the installation instructions for its supported configuration format.",
